@jamorham You're doing perfect work, this is your version of Aug. 20th. It now shows me active insulin, ampule remaining amount, and battery status. I have a question at the beginning of the line U: 0 what is this?

Ask a question you can install from Smartguard the Next calibration time in display? And The Sensor End TimeDays and hours would be that available for display in xDrip? Thank you for request.

![20991491_1598810380170122_731774621_o](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/22836158/29494603-105c5062-85ae-11e7-8495-44414ec410b7.png)

@Aquarius83mn I think the first U:0 will be from another status line option you have enabled, perhaps total treatment insulin which is not data coming from the pump.

@AdrianLxM The 640G uploader app would need to be modified to include that extra data in the broadcast. Within reason I can add xDrip support for whatever data is presented via the intent.

@willflach The active insulin number is a mathematical estimate from the pump of what it thinks the insulin will be doing in the body. How many units of insulin would you have in a typical bolus? Is 2 decimal places needed or is this request to match with a figure displayed elsewhere?

This sound wunderful. I' ve got one more question...I can't stop the alarm. How does it works?I press the silence but it doesn't works.Many greets meike



